Descriptions taken from the manuals
-----------------------------------

Each companion says what a control does in the manual's own words, quoted and
attributed to the printed page it came from rather than rewritten. That text is
its maker's, not ours:

  Chase Bliss Lost + Found   the twenty-four mode descriptions, the per-mode
                             tips and the knob descriptions — roughly 1,400
                             words. Copyright Chase Bliss Audio.

  Strymon Volante            the knob and switch descriptions, quoted by
                             printed page — roughly 550 words. Copyright
                             Strymon.

  Fulltone OCD-Germanium     the knob and HP/LP descriptions, and passages from
                             Michael Fuller's letter on page 1 — roughly 700
                             words. Copyright Fulltone.

The rest of each page — the drawing of the enclosure, the working model of what
the controls do to timing or gain, the index of the printed manual, and the
notes marked as inferred rather than documented — was written for this site and
is covered by the MIT licence.

No manual is reproduced here in full, and there is no PDF in this repository.
Every link at a manual opens the maker's own copy of it.


Product photographs
-------------------

The homepage carries one photograph of each pedal, downloaded from that maker's
own site and normalized for the shelf: background removed, trimmed to the
pedal, centred on a common canvas at a common scale.

  images/chase-bliss-lost-and-found.webp   Chase Bliss Audio
  images/strymon-volante.webp              Strymon
  images/fulltone-ocd-germanium.webp       Fulltone

Each remains the property of its maker, and is used here only to identify the
pedal whose companion sits behind it.


